ments if  you had any late payments maybe you paid  for a mobile phone or a utility bill if  you paid for it late and it's now  flagging up on your credit file then  what I would recommend doing is just  ring up the company that you paid late  and ask them what you need to do to  rectify the situation just ring up the  companies and make sure that you have no  outstanding payments it's so annoying  because sometimes it can be as little as  11 pound fifth day and then that stops  you them buying a property which is  going to make you thousands of  four pounds so always make sure that  you've paid off any late payments bring  up the companies number six is use  credit sometimes people who want a good  credit they think that if they have no  credit cards they have no debts they  have no loans it's going to mean that  they have better credit somehow but it's  actually the opposite what banks and  lenders want to see when they check your  credit file is they want to see that  you're a responsible adult they want to  see that you have actually got credit  you've got credit cards you've got loans  but you just always pay back on time and  responsibly and that actually helps  improve your credit number seven don't  be stubborn what I mean by that is  sometimes companies do make mistakes I  had a situation where my I counseled my  phone bill it's always phones we do this  I counseled my phone bill and even  though I count to it they carried on  charging me and I was like this is  ridiculous and I kept trying accounts  like couldnt get hold of them so then I  just cancelled the direct debit I don't  know exactly what happened but I know  that about three years later apparently  I think that company were wrong  I owned an one month's bill a 56 pound  apparently I think they were wrong  because I've been trying to counsel for  months and months and that was now  affecting my ability to buy a house and  I was thinking oh my goodness so I  tracked it back to this phone company  and I went into the store and I said  look you know I didn't owe this money I  like I was proving to them I didn't area  but they were just I don't know I'm not  sure you know the human nature and they  wanted to fight the case and say look do  you know how hard it is to cancel with  you guys you know I tried to counsel for  months I'd finished and I knew that I  was right and I had a proof of that and  email everything to prove that but in  the end I just thought what's the point  if I fight this it could take months and  months then my house is gonna fall  through all because I was stubborn so  don't be super stubborn just think  commercially and again pay off things  that need to be paid off and don't be  stupid number eight this is a really  really important tip if like me you're a  landlord know lots of houses sometimes  what can happen and it's really  frustrating when this happens is I pay  little bounce so at one of your houses  and you might have lots of different  lenders they'll go to try and take money  out  your account and for whatever reason  because you've managed your money badly  there's no money in that account and for  the sake of one hundred and fifty pounds  for that monthly payment it then bounces  there's no money now you might have  twenty thousand a million pounds in your  other accounts but in this account you  happen to have no money and it bounced  now that can really badly affect your  credit I know I had that happen to me  once when they tried to take a payment I  didn't have money in that account so  that they didn't take the payment so  what I did was I asked the lender I said  listen  can I please give you 150 pounds one  months just to sort of sit in like your  inner is in it with you in a reserve  camp if you ever can take the payment  from me I'm good for it I do have the  money  use that one hundred and fifty pounds  and then find me and tell me and I'll  give you another hundred fifty pounds so  it just kind of just sits there in this  in this part and after doing that I did  that with all my lenders I just gave  them all I was always a month ahead so  that if they can't take it there's a  little pot and I'm sure that that's  probably saved me big-time in any in any  bouncing the light payments so really  important if you're a property investor  number nine is if there's anything  really weird showing on your credit file  on Credit Karma  and it's affecting you quit and you  don't understand it ask Credit Karma to  investigate for you don't just accept oh  I've got really bad credit if you don't  know why it's it's small you can usually  always rectify it so you know fight it  and find out if there's an error which  there can be sometimes there's errors  and it's saying you've got bad credit  just because of something that's  happened which is not your fault so  always ask things to be to be disputed  and and fight your corner and number ten  is when you are applying for loans don't  apply for lots and lots of loans all at  once because when you do that every time  you apply for credit what happens is it  leaves a print on your credit file  there's nothing wrong with having print  but if you've got lots of them  particularly if they're all close  together it makes it look like you're  desperate for money you're like Sheila  Munich I need a loan then that affects  your credit so don't be getting loads of  quotes the loans in the space of a short  time over and over if you are getting  quotes or mortgages and stuff  ask the question is this going to leave  a print on my credit  and just be mindful of that don't have  to go overboard and be crazy there's  nothing wrong with having prints we  don't want loads of prints all in one go  so those are the 10 things that will  help improve your credit there is a  bonus tip as well and that is to be  patient it does sometimes take time  you're not going to go from 500 up to  710 in the space of a few days or even a  few weeks this can take months but you  can rectify a big problem quickly which  can help you get financed so just be  patient don't write yourself off either  I've known many of my students who are  wanting to get properties they've got  even if got CC J's County Court  judgments against them they've got a  really bad credit but it doesn't  necessarily mean you can't get a  mortgage because if you're buying a  property to rent out of course they care  about your credit but more than anything  they care about the property and is the  property profitable their lending on the  property they're not lending it to you  so don't write yourself off get a good  broker be patient and I wish you all the  best in having an excellent credit and  being a successful property investor  [Music]

